<LanguageData>
  <VME_AgnosticismDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: story(priority=-999)->-->
    <li>story(priority=-999)-&gt;</li>
    <!--EN: setup->[founderName] made us see that the existence of God, of the divine and the supernatural, is unknown and unknowable.-->
    <li>setup-&gt;[founderName]让我们看到上帝的存在，神圣的和超自然的，是未知的和不可知的。</li>
    <!--EN: setup->[founderName] was the first to realize that we didn't need Gods to explain the Universe.-->
    <li>setup-&gt;[founderName] 是第一个意识到我们不需要神来解释宇宙的人。</li>
    <!--EN: setup->Struck by the non-spiritual nature of the world, [founderName] studied history and philosophy and discovered the new truth that guides us.-->
    <li>setup-&gt;受到世界非精神本质的震撼，[founderName]研究历史和哲学，发现了指导我们的新真理。</li>
    <!--EN: setup->During an ancient ritual, [founderName] began to question the validity of [founder_possessive] former beliefs. Why put your whole life in service of an unknowable God?-->
    <li>setup-&gt;在一次古老的仪式中，[founderName]开始质疑[founder_possessive]以前信仰的有效性。为什么要把你的一生奉献给一个不可知的上帝呢？</li>
    <!--EN: setup->[founderName]'s tough life had made [founder_objective] reject [founder_possessive] faith. Gods are unknowable and should have no bearing on a person's day to day.-->
    <li>setup-&gt;[founderName]的艰难生活使[founder_objective]拒绝了[founder_possessive]信仰。神是不可知的，不应该影响一个人的日常生活。</li>
    <!--EN: story(uses=1,priority=-10)->The [memberNamePlural] would still be worshipping ancient spirits without [founderName]'s teachings, and thus [founder_pronoun] will always be remembered amongst our people as: [honorific].-->
    <li>story(uses=1,priority=-10)-&gt;如果没有[founderName]的教义，[memberNamePlural]仍然会崇拜远古神灵，因此[founder_pronoun]将永远被我们的人民铭记为：[honorific]。</li>
    <!--EN: story(uses=1,priority=-10)->[founderName]'s speech at a [ritualName] inspired many to lead a [memeAdjective] life, free of the shackles of magical thinking. Thus [founder_pronoun] will always be remembered amongst our people as: [honorific].-->
    <li>story(uses=1,priority=-10)-&gt;[founderName] 在 [ritualName] 上的演讲激励许多人过上 [memeAdjective] 的生活，摆脱魔法思维的束缚。因此，[founder_pronoun] 将永远被我们人民铭记为：[honorific]。</li>
    <!--EN: story(uses=1,priority=-10)->[founderName] will always be remembered amongst our people as [honorific]: The one that forever banished magical thinking from our minds.-->
    <li>story(uses=1,priority=-10)-&gt;[founderName] 将永远被我们人民铭记为 [honorific]：永远 将魔法思维从我们的头脑中驱逐出去。</li>
    <!--EN: honorific->The Godkiller-->
    <li>honorific-&gt;弑神者</li>
    <!--EN: honorific->The Atheist-->
    <li>honorific-&gt;无神论者</li>
    <!--EN: honorific->The Agnostic-->
    <li>honorific-&gt;不可知论者</li>
    <!--EN: honorific->The Disenter-->
    <li>honorific-&gt;异议者</li>
    <!--EN: honorific->The Light in the Dark-->
    <li>honorific-&gt;黑暗中的光明</li>
    <!--EN: honorific->The Unbeliever-->
    <li>honorific-&gt;不信者</li>
    <!--EN: honorific->The Heretic-->
    <li>honorific-&gt;异教徒</li>
  </VME_AgnosticismDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
  <VME_AuthoritarianDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: lesson(priority=-1)->stuff happens-->
    <li>lesson(priority=-1)-&gt;事情发生了</li>
    <!--EN: r_pattern->"[r_lessonIntro] [r_lessonMain]. [r_lessonReinforcement]"\n\n  - [lessonAttribution]-->
    <li>r_pattern-&gt;“[r_lessonIntro] [r_lessonMain]。[r_lessonReinforcement]”

 - [lessonAttribution]</li>
    <!--EN: lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull], on a [speechadjective] [speech] on the [TerrainFeature]-->
    <li>lessonAttribution-&gt;[founder_nameFull]，在 [speechadjective] [speech] 上，在 [TerrainFeature] 上</li>
    <!--EN: lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull], [speechadjective] [speech] in the [Community]-->
    <li>lessonAttribution-&gt;[founder_nameFull]、[speechadjective] [speech] 在 [Community] 中</li>
    <!--EN: speechadjective->rousing-->
    <li>speechadjective-&gt;振奋人心</li>
    <!--EN: speechadjective->public-->
    <li>speechadjective-&gt;公众</li>
    <!--EN: speechadjective->multitudinous-->
    <li>speechadjective-&gt;众多</li>
    <!--EN: speechadjective->political-->
    <li>speechadjective-&gt;政治</li>
    <!--EN: speechadjective->passionate-->
    <li>speechadjective-&gt;热情</li>
    <!--EN: speechadjective->fiery-->
    <li>speechadjective-&gt;火热</li>
    <!--EN: speech->Speech-->
    <li>speech-&gt;演讲</li>
    <!--EN: speech->Address-->
    <li>speech-&gt;地址</li>
    <!--EN: speech->Disquisition-->
    <li>speech-&gt;专题讨论</li>
    <!--EN: speech->Declamation-->
    <li>speech-&gt;宣言</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->The entire struggle for survival is a conquest of the means of existence.-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;整个生存斗争就是对生存手段的征服。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->I also extend noble respects to the revolutionary martyrs, both sung and unsung, who sacrificed their precious lives in the sacred war for achieving the reunification and independence of our people.-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;我还要向在神圣战争中为实现我国人民的统一和独立而献出宝贵生命的有名的和无名的革命烈士致以崇高的敬意。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->We cannot think of our people today without remembering the sweats and blood shed by the generation of the victors in the war, the great spirit they demonstrated and the ennobling sacrifice of the warriors.-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;今天，我们不能不记住战争胜利者一代所流下的汗水和鲜血、他们所表现出的伟大精神以及战士们的崇高牺牲。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->There is only one order. It is categorical and obligatory for every one. It already wings over and enflames hearts from [place_name] to corners of this world: Conquer!-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;只有一个订单。它对每个人来说都是绝对的和强制性的。它已经展翅飞翔，将 [place_name] 的心点燃到这个世界的各个角落：征服！</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->Nothing is possible unless one will commands, a will which has to be obeyed by others, beginning at the top and ending only at the very bottom.-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;除非一个人愿意发号施令，否则一切皆有可能，这是一种必须由其他人服从的意志，从顶部开始到最底部结束。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->My fellow-countrymen, man does not exist on theories and phrases, on declarations or on systems of political philosophy; he lives on what he can gain from the soil by his own labor.-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;我的同胞们，人不是存在于理论和短语、宣言或政治哲学体系上；而是存在于政治哲学体系中。他靠自己的劳动从土地中获得的东西为生。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->Our victory was the victory of the ennobling patriotism and mass heroism of our citizens, the victory of justice and progress over injustice and reaction, the future of mankind over our enemies.-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;我们的胜利是我们公民崇高的爱国主义和群众英雄主义的胜利，是正义和进步战胜非正义和反动的胜利，是人类未来战胜敌人的胜利。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->To those who can hear me, I say - do not despair-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;我对那些能听到我说话的人说 - 不要绝望</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->No one will be astonished if now, when this phase may be considered overcome, we throw off whatever and whoever would like to deflect us from marching toward fulfillment of our movement-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;如果现在，当这一阶段可以被认为已经克服时，如果我们抛弃任何想要阻止我们向实现我们的运动前进的人或事，没有人会感到惊讶</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->We are actors in a new era in which we can have no truck with the mentality of the past-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;我们是新时代的演员，不能再跟过去的心态发生关系</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->Youth marched conscious of its historic responsibility toward a goal sensed but not clearly defined-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;青年人意识到自己的历史责任，朝着一个已感知但尚未明确界定的目标迈进</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->In these days our generations are not merely faced with territorial and political problems, but also with supreme issues of the existence of our faith, our civilization and our culture, which are now at stake once more-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;如今，我们这一代人不仅面临领土和政治问题，还面临着我们的信仰、我们的文明和我们的文化的存在的最高问题，这些问题现在再次受到威胁</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->Certain people wished to be in our ranks in order to create among us a controlling body or a new minority group. That could not be permitted-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;某些人希望加入我们的行列，以便在我们中间建立一个控制机构或一个新的少数群体。这是不被允许的</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->Together, we will march towards the dawn of a new era.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;我们将共同迈向新时代的黎明。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->Our future is bright, and we will persevere.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;我们的未来是光明的，我们会坚持下去。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->Whatever projects there may exist now, the historic destiny of our era will be settled.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;无论现在存在什么计划，我们时代的历史命运都将被确定。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->For this reason, because we know that ours is the truth, and because we have labored for it endlessly, we look upon events with serenity.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;因此，因为我们知道我们的真理是真理，并且因为我们为之不懈努力，所以我们平静地看待事件。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->We have called you together to carry our work to completion, for it is heralded by continuous triumphs.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;我们召集你们一起完成我们的工作，因为它预示着持续的胜利。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->It is not enough to set our goal. It must be pursued with constancy and sacrifice.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;仅仅设定我们的目标是不够的。必须坚持不懈并做出牺牲来追求它。</li>
  </VME_AuthoritarianDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
  <VME_ChthonianDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: chthonianBasis   ->There are vast entities in this world that defy any explanation. Concepts far more ancient than mere Gods.-->
    <li>chthonianBasis   -&gt;这个世界上存在着无法解释的巨大实体。概念比单纯的神要古老得多。</li>
    <!--EN: chthonianBasis   ->Beyond the Veil, a whole new universe of insanity-inducing Old Gods awaits.-->
    <li>chthonianBasis   -&gt;在面纱之外，一个由令人疯狂的旧神组成的全新宇宙正在等待着。</li>
    <!--EN: chthonianBasis   ->Gods are not the ultimate predator in the Universe, for there are ancient entities far more powerful. Entities that should be respected... and feared.-->
    <li>chthonianBasis   -&gt;神并不是宇宙中的终极掠食者，因为还有更强大的远古实体。应该尊重和恐惧的实体。</li>
    <!--EN: chthonianBasis   ->In the unknown vastness of space, there are insane entities that could remake the whole Universe with a simple wayward thought.-->
    <li>chthonianBasis   -&gt;在未知的浩瀚空间中，存在着一些疯狂的实体，它们可以通过简单任性的想法重塑整个宇宙。</li>
    <!--EN: chthonianFact    ->We are like insects to these entities. Not even worthy of their attention. As insignificant to them as an ant would be to us.-->
    <li>chthonianFact    -&gt;对于这些实体来说，我们就像昆虫。甚至不值得他们关注。对于他们来说，就像一只蚂蚁对于我们来说是微不足道的。</li>
    <!--EN: chthonianFact    ->They do not care about humanity. We are nothing to them. Not even a footnote.-->
    <li>chthonianFact    -&gt;他们不关心人性。我们对他们来说什么都不是。连脚注都没有。</li>
    <!--EN: chthonianFact    ->Though powerful, they are uncaring. So far beyond our intelligence that we are not even sapient in their eyes.-->
    <li>chthonianFact    -&gt;虽然强大，但他们漠不关心。远远超出了我们的智力，在他们眼里我们甚至算不上聪明。</li>
    <!--EN: chthonianFact    ->From their point of view, we don't even exist. The same way you don't think about the microbes in the surface of the chair you are sitting on.-->
    <li>chthonianFact    -&gt;从他们的角度来看，我们甚至不存在。就像你不会考虑你所坐的椅子表面的微生物一样。</li>
    <!--EN: chthonianProphecy->[weMustBe] careful, for it wouldn't be wise to attract their attention, as they could destroy us in an instant.-->
    <li>chthonianProphecy-&gt;[weMustBe]小心，因为吸引他们的注意力并不明智，因为他们可能会在瞬间内摧毁我们。</li>
    <!--EN: chthonianProphecy->[byWorshipping] them, perhaps we can avoid their gaze.-->
    <li>chthonianProphecy-&gt;[byWorshipping]他们，也许我们可以避开他们的目光。</li>
    <!--EN: chthonianProphecy->Don't be fooled: they don't deserve our devotion. But perhaps by showing a false façade of piety we can avoid their attention long enough.-->
    <li>chthonianProphecy-&gt;不要被愚弄：他们不值得我们奉献。但也许通过表现出虔诚的虚假外表，我们可以足够长时间地避免他们的注意。</li>
    <!--EN: chthonianProphecy->Even so, a lot can be learned from them. Eldritch knowledge awaits those brave -or foolish- enough to peek into the screaming visage of madness.-->
    <li>chthonianProphecy-&gt;即便如此，我们还是可以从他们身上学到很多东西。可怕的知识等待着那些勇敢——或者愚蠢——的人来窥探疯狂的尖叫面孔。</li>
    <!--EN: weMustBe->We must be-->
    <li>weMustBe-&gt;我们必须</li>
    <!--EN: weMustBe->It is imperative that we are-->
    <li>weMustBe-&gt;我们必须</li>
    <!--EN: weMustBe->We'd better be-->
    <li>weMustBe-&gt;我们最好</li>
    <!--EN: byWorshipping->By worshipping-->
    <li>byWorshipping-&gt;通过崇拜</li>
    <!--EN: byWorshipping->We hope if we worshop-->
    <li>byWorshipping-&gt;我们希望如果我们崇拜</li>
  </VME_ChthonianDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
  <VME_CorporateDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: episodeCorporate(priority=-1)->-->
    <li>episodeCorporate(priority=-1)-&gt;</li>
    <!--EN: r_pattern->"To: All Employees\n\nFrom: Upper Management\n\nSubject: [subject]\n\n[r_introMemo] [r_episodeCorporate] [r_episodeCorporate]"-->
    <li>r_pattern-&gt;“致：所有员工

发件人：高层管理人员

主题：[subject]

[r_introMemo][r_episodeCorporate][r_episodeCorporate]”</li>
    <!--EN: introMemo->Coworkers, it has come to my attention that many in the office have been spending time doing unapproved activities.-->
    <li>introMemo-&gt;同事们，我注意到办公室里的许多人一直在花时间从事未经批准的活动。</li>
    <!--EN: introMemo->This is to remind the division that, starting today, we are now filing all Testing Procedure Specification (TPS) reports with new cover sheets.-->
    <li>introMemo-&gt;谨此提醒该部门，从今天开始，我们将使用新的封面页归档所有测试程序规范 (TPS) 报告。</li>
    <!--EN: introMemo->In our efforts to make your orientation a pleasant one, we have implemented an employee self-service system to assist you in completing the new hire process, including benefits enrollment.-->
    <li>introMemo-&gt;为了让您的入职培训变得愉快，我们实施了员工自助服务系统，以帮助您完成新聘用流程，包括福利登记。</li>
    <!--EN: introMemo->As you know, tomorrow afternoon we’ll be meeting to discuss the status of all of our current projects.-->
    <li>introMemo-&gt;如您所知，明天下午我们将开会讨论当前所有项目的状态。</li>
    <!--EN: introMemo->For tomorrow’s 3 p.m. staff meeting in the conference room, please bring 5 copies of the aforementioned materials.-->
    <li>introMemo-&gt;明天下午 3 点员工在会议室开会时，请携带上述材料5份。</li>
    <!--EN: introMemo->Due to your excellent performance in the last year —especially your work in the Northwest Region!— we would like to feature you as one of our spotlight employees.-->
    <li>introMemo-&gt;由于您在过去一年中的出色表现，尤其是您在西北地区的工作！——我们谨将您列为我们的重点员工之一。</li>
    <!--EN: introMemo->Do you know the #1 thing that matters most to our customers? Money, of course.-->
    <li>introMemo-&gt;您知道对我们的客户来说最重要的第一件事吗？当然是钱。</li>
    <!--EN: introMemo->Are you using the 3 most useful collaboration tools?. We'd really appreciate it if you get those synergies flowing.-->
    <li>introMemo-&gt;您在使用 3 种最有用的协作工具吗？如果您能发挥这些协同作用，我们将不胜感激。</li>
    <!--EN: introMemo->Good morning. There are some exciting changes coming to our department that I wish to alert you to.-->
    <li>introMemo-&gt;早上好。我们部门即将发生一些令人兴奋的变化，我想提醒您注意。</li>
    <!--EN: introMemo->I am very pleased that you have accepted our offer and are joining our team.-->
    <li>introMemo-&gt;我很高兴您接受了我们的邀请并加入我们的团队。</li>
    <!--EN: introMemo->We are very happy to have you as a part of our team. The staff here is looking forward to helping you fill the management void we have had for some time.-->
    <li>introMemo-&gt;我们很高兴您成为我们团队的一员。这里的工作人员期待帮助您填补我们一段时间以来的管理空白。</li>
    <!--EN: episodeCorporate(uses=1)->This memo is a reminder to use your work hours for work.-->
    <li>episodeCorporate(uses=1)-&gt;此备忘录旨在提醒您利用工作时间进行工作。</li>
    <!--EN: episodeCorporate(uses=1)->Of course, we don't want you to view our organization as a place of drudgery and draconian rules. We encourage a fun and competitive environment.-->
    <li>episodeCorporate(uses=1)-&gt;当然，我们不希望您将我们的组织视为一个充满苦差事和严酷规则的地方。我们鼓励营造有趣和竞争的环境。</li>
    <!--EN: episodeCorporate(uses=1)->Though this change may initially seem like a headache and an extra step, it is necessary to ensure the proper functioning of our company.-->
    <li>episodeCorporate(uses=1)-&gt;虽然这一变化乍一看似乎令人头疼并且是一个额外的步骤，但它对于确保我们公司的正常运作是必要的。</li>
    <!--EN: episodeCorporate(uses=1)->Please be sure to follow this new procedure.-->
    <li>episodeCorporate(uses=1)-&gt;请务必遵循此新程序。</li>
    <!--EN: episodeCorporate(uses=1)->I think I don't need to remind you all that we are a team, no, a family. And families stick together, no matter the challenge.-->
    <li>episodeCorporate(uses=1)-&gt;我想我不需要提醒大家，我们是一个团队，不，是一个家庭。无论面临什么挑战，家人都会团结在一起。</li>
    <!--EN: episodeCorporate(uses=1)->This critical issue will be discussed in an all-hands meeting, ASAP.-->
    <li>episodeCorporate(uses=1)-&gt; 这一关键问题将尽快在全体会议上讨论。</li>
    <!--EN: episodeCorporate(uses=1)->It is prioritary that we start thinking outside the box. And let's all sing from the same hymn sheet.-->
    <li>episodeCorporate(uses=1)-&gt;我们首先要开始跳出框框思考。让我们都唱同一张赞美诗。</li>
    <!--EN: episodeCorporate(uses=1)->Let's take it to the next level, people.-->
    <li>episodeCorporate(uses=1)-&gt;各位，让我们更进一步吧。</li>
    <!--EN: episodeCorporate(uses=1)->Our executive management has decided that some restructuring of our department is in order so that our transition through this merger can be as seamless as possible. You'll receive more info shortly.-->
    <li>episodeCorporate(uses=1)-&gt;我们的执行管理层已决定对我们的部门进行一些重组，以便我们通过这次合并进行的过渡能够尽可能顺利。您很快就会收到更多信息。</li>
    <!--EN: episodeCorporate(uses=1)->We are scheduling a staff meeting for tomorrow from 12 pm to 1 pm where we will outline the steps of this important transition; lunch will be provided.-->
    <li>episodeCorporate(uses=1)-&gt;我们计划于明天中午 12 点至下午 1 点召开一次员工会议，届时我们将概述这一重要过渡的步骤；将提供午餐。</li>
    <!--EN: episodeCorporate(uses=1)->Your experience and vision will be a great asset to this group, and I know that the team is looking forward to working with you.-->
    <li>episodeCorporate(uses=1)-&gt;您的经验和远见将成为该团队的宝贵财富，我知道该团队期待与您合作。</li>
    <!--EN: subject->Inappropriate use of time on Google Doodle games-->
    <li>subject-&gt;在 Google Doodle 游戏上不当使用时间</li>
    <!--EN: subject->Please reload ink on the printer once it runs out-->
    <li>subject-&gt;墨水用完后请在打印机上重新装入墨水</li>
    <!--EN: subject->Fall Clothes Line Promotion-->
    <li>subject-&gt;秋季服装系列促销</li>
    <!--EN: subject->Don't invite Steve to the meeting. He'll dress like a ghost-->
    <li>subject-&gt;不要邀请 Steve 参加会议。他会穿得像个幽灵</li>
    <!--EN: subject->Warning: Unattended items in your desks may be stolen. The Company is not responsible for your belongings-->
    <li>subject-&gt;警告：办公桌上无人看管的物品可能会被盗。本公司不对您的财物负责</li>
    <!--EN: subject->Office Memo to All Employees-->
    <li>subject-&gt;致所有员工的办公室备忘录</li>
    <!--EN: subject->Restroom Use Policy-->
