    <li>lessonAttribution-&gt;[founder_nameFull]，就在执行之前</li>
    <!--EN: lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull], [speech] on the [TerrainFeature]-->
    <li>lessonAttribution-&gt;[founder_nameFull]、[speech] 在 [TerrainFeature]</li>
    <!--EN: lessonAttribution->[founder_nameFull], [speech] in the [Community]-->
    <li>lessonAttribution-&gt;[founder_nameFull]、[speech] 在 [Community] 中</li>
    <!--EN: attributionSource->[memeConcept]-->
    <li>attributionSource-&gt;[memeConcept]</li>
    <!--EN: attributionSource->[memeAdjective] [memeConcept]-->
    <li>attributionSource-&gt;[memeAdjective] [memeConcept]</li>
    <!--EN: attributionSource->A [memeAdjective] Life-->
    <li>attributionSource-&gt;[memeAdjective] 生命</li>
    <!--EN: attributionSource->Reflections by a [attributionJob]-->
    <li>attributionSource-&gt;[attributionJob]的反思</li>
    <!--EN: attributionSource->Journal of a [attributionJob]-->
    <li>attributionSource-&gt;[attributionJob] 的日记</li>
    <!--EN: attributionSource->Thoughts of a [attributionJob]-->
    <li>attributionSource-&gt;[attributionJob] 的想法</li>
    <!--EN: attributionSource->Life of a [attributionJob]-->
    <li>attributionSource-&gt;[attributionJob] 的生活</li>
    <!--EN: attributionJob->[memeAdjective] [place_job]-->
    <li>attributionJob-&gt;[memeAdjective] [place_job]</li>
    <!--EN: attributionJob->[place_job]-->
    <li>attributionJob-&gt;[place_job]</li>
    <!--EN: speech->Speech-->
    <li>speech-&gt;演讲</li>
    <!--EN: speech->Address-->
    <li>speech-&gt;地址</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->After so many sleepless nights of careful deliberation, I came to a simple conclussion:-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;经过这么多个不眠之夜的仔细思考，我得出了一个简单的结论：</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->What is a fundamental truth of human existence?-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;人类存在的基本真理是什么？</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->I have suffered a lot in this life. But this suffering has taught me a simple principle:-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;我这一生受了很多苦。但这次痛苦教会了我一个简单的原则：</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->Growing in squalor on the [place_summary] [place_name], I learned a sincere axiom:-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;在[place_summary][place_name]的肮脏中成长，我学到了一条真诚的公理：</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->Internalize this lesson, for it will serve you well:-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;将本课程内化，因为它将对您很有帮助：</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->Are you feeling lost? Perhaps you haven't yet figured out this very simple concept:-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;你感到失落吗？也许你还没有弄清楚这个非常简单的概念：</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->They tried to tempt me with a life of rich, dull productivity, but they couldn't fool me:-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;他们试图用丰富而乏味的生产力来诱惑我，但他们骗不了我：</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->pleasure, the satisfaction of bodily desires, is the highest good and proper aim of human life. Whether through religion or philosophy our entire lives should be focused on enjoying ourselves as much as possible-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;快乐，即身体欲望的满足，是人类生活的最高善和适当目标。无论是通过宗教还是哲学，我们的整个生活都应该专注于尽可能地享受自己</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->I finally figured out the only reason to be alive is to enjoy it-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;我终于明白活着的唯一理由就是享受它</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->the only way to get rid of temptation is to yield to it-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;摆脱诱惑的唯一方法就是屈服于诱惑</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->salvation is for the feeble. I don't want salvation, I want life, all of life, the miserable as well as the superb-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;救赎是为软弱的人准备的。我不想要拯救，我想要生命，所有的生命，悲惨的和美好的</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->pleasure is not a need, but an incentive-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;快乐不是一种需要，而是一种激励</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->the most responsible way of life right now is to enjoy ourselves while we can-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;现在最负责任的生活方式就是趁我们还可以的时候尽情享受</li>
    <!--EN: lessonMain->you can live to be a hundred if you give up all the things that make you want to live to be a hundred-->
    <li>lessonMain-&gt;如果你放弃所有让你想活到一百岁的东西，你就能活到一百岁</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->No one can argue with that.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;没有人可以反驳这一点。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->Only fools think otherwise.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;只有傻瓜才会不这么认为。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->And as we now know, that was soon to become evident to everyone.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;正如我们现在所知，这一点很快就为所有人所了解。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->Everything that has happened since has reinforced that fact.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;此后发生的一切都强化了这一事实。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->It is as if that is etched directly into my mind.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;这就像直接铭刻在我的脑海里一样。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->It is something I'll never forget.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;这是我永远不会忘记的事情。</li>
  </VME_HedonistDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
  <VME_OmnismDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: episode(priority=-1)->-->
    <li>episode(priority=-1)-&gt;</li>
    <!--EN: creation->It is limiting beyond words to bind oneself to any particular god or belief. The combined gifts of all supreme beings, philosophers and forces is what should truly be appreciated.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;将自己束缚于任何特定的神或信仰是无法言喻的限制。所有至高无上的存在、哲学家和力量的综合恩赐才是真正值得欣赏的。</li>
    <!--EN: creation->All religions and ideologies point to the whole truth, that a single transcendent purpose unites all things.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;所有宗教和意识形态都指向全部真理，即单一的超越目的将所有事物团结在一起。</li>
    <!--EN: creation->It seems that the teachings of the ancient [religion] and [religion2] scholars had a lot of truth to teach us.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;古代[religion]和[religion2]学者的教义似乎有很多真理可以教给我们。</li>
    <!--EN: creation->Truth can be found in all religions and ideologies, as they are all part of the greater human experience. Whether it is the teachings of the [religion] texts or the philosophies of the ancient [religion2] scholars, we can learn about the universe by opening our minds to this truth.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;真理可以在所有宗教和意识形态中找到，因为它们都是更伟大的人类经验的一部分。无论是[religion]文献的教义，还是古代[religion2]学者的哲学，我们都可以通过敞开心扉接受这个真理来了解宇宙。</li>
    <!--EN: creation->Human beings are inquisitive creatures, and as such we have invented some incredible concepts: either [religion] teachings or [religion2] tennets hold a portion of the complete truth, and as such all beliefs are intrinsically true and useful.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;人类是好奇的生物，因此我们发明了一些令人难以置信的概念：[religion]教义或[religion2]信条包含了完整真理的一部分，因此所有信念本质上都是真实且有用的。</li>
    <!--EN: creation->All religions and ideologies are legitimate. A single transcendent purpose unites all things and people, and you can reach this universal purpose by any means, either by the study of the ancient [religion] texts or by following the [religion2] dogma.-->
    <li>creation-&gt;所有宗教和意识形态都是合法的。一个单一的超越目的将所有事物和人类联合起来，您可以通过任何方式实现这个普遍目的，无论是通过研究古代 [religion] 文本还是遵循 [religion2] 教条。</li>
    <!--EN: episode(uses=1)->Only through carefully studying all beliefs can we truly understand the nature of reality.-->
    <li>episode(uses=1)-&gt;只有仔细研究所有信念，我们才能真正理解现实的本质。</li>
    <!--EN: episode(uses=1)->We must recognize that all religions contain varying elements of a common truth, and respect all beliefs accordingly.-->
    <li>episode(uses=1)-&gt;我们必须认识到所有宗教都包含共同真理的不同要素，并相应地尊重所有信仰。</li>
    <!--EN: religion->Christian-->
    <li>religion-&gt;基督教</li>
    <!--EN: religion->Buddhist-->
    <li>religion-&gt;佛教</li>
    <!--EN: religion->Muslim-->
