    <!--EN: speech->Meditation Speech-->
    <li>speech-&gt;冥想演讲</li>
    <!--EN: speech->Know-Yourself Address-->
    <li>speech-&gt;了解自己的地址</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->I always repeat, "letting go is the hardest asana":-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;我总是重复，“放手是最难的体式”：</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->It took me long years of intense meditation to understand that-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;我经过多年的深入冥想才明白</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->We must not be like the [foeLeader], who don't know themselves. Observing them did teach me one thing:-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;我们不能像[foeLeader]一样，不了解自己。观察他们确实教会了我一件事：</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->By teaching Yoga on the [place_summary] [place_name], I realized that-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;通过在 [place_summary] [place_name] 上教授瑜伽，我意识到</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->Find your center and set intentions for the day as you begin to focus on your breath – body connection. You will then realize that-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;当您开始关注呼吸与身体的联系时，找到您的中心并设定当天的目标。然后你就会意识到</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->You must start with a series of breath to movement flows, energizing and invigorating the body and the mind. And you will finally know that-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;您必须从一系列呼吸运动开始，为身体和心灵注入能量和活力。你最终会知道</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->A flower does not think of competing to the flower next to it. It just blooms. One thing will become increasingly clear then: that-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;一朵花不会想到与它旁边的花竞争。它刚刚绽放。到那时，一件事就会变得越来越清楚：</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->You will begin the journey of the self, through the self, to the self. Then you'll see that-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;你将开始自我之旅，穿越自我，到达自我。然后你会看到</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->You cannot always control what goes on outside. But you can always control what goes on inside. Once that is achieved you will see that-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;您无法始终控制外面发生的事情。但您始终可以控制内部发生的事情。一旦实现了这一点，你就会看到</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->The longest journey of any person is the journey inward. This journey shows you that-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;任何人最长的旅程都是向内的旅程。这次旅程向您展示了</li>
    <!--EN: lessonIntro->Truth lies in pursuing a spiritual philosophy without adherence to a religion, personal growth and inner peace of an individual are more important than a relationship with the divine, and thus-->
    <li>lessonIntro-&gt;真理在于追求精神哲学而不是信仰宗教，个人的成长和内心的平静比与神圣的关系更重要，因此</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->Just breathe.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;呼吸即可。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->Be where you are, not where you think you should be.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;呆在你所在的地方，而不是你认为你应该在的地方。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->The pose begins when you want to leave it.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;当您想要离开时，该姿势开始。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->Inhale the future, exhale the past.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;吸入未来，呼出过去。</li>
    <!--EN: lessonReinforcement->It's not about being good at something. It's about being good to yourself.-->
    <li>lessonReinforcement-&gt;这与擅长某件事无关。这是关于对自己好一点。</li>
  </VME_SecularSpiritualityDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
  <VME_SerketistDescription.rules.rulesStrings>
    <!--EN: serketistBasis   ->There is no higher lifeform than the Hive Queens. Their nourishing jelly is like ambrosia, and the entire world should be remade in their image.-->
    <li>serketistBasis   -&gt;没有比蜂后更高的生命形式了。他们的营养果冻就像甘露，整个世界都应该按照他们的形象重塑。</li>
    <!--EN: serketistBasis   ->In its hubris, humanity accidentally stumbled upon the creation of the perfect lifeform: Insectoids.-->
    <li>serketistBasis   -&gt;在狂妄自大中，人类意外地创造了完美的生命形式：昆虫。</li>
    <!--EN: serketistBasis   ->The runaway creation of some forgotten ancient geneticist, Insectoids have evolved to become the perfect lifeform.-->
    <li>serketistBasis   -&gt;昆虫是某个被遗忘的古代遗传学家的失控创造，已经进化成为完美的生命形式。</li>
    <!--EN: serketistBasis   ->Threatened by the Mechanoid menace, mankind engineered the perfect lifeform: Insectoids.-->
    <li>serketistBasis   -&gt;受到机械人的威胁，人类设计了完美的生命形式：昆虫。</li>
    <!--EN: serketistBasis   ->Led by the sacred Hive Queens, Insectoids are the perfect lifeform in the galaxy.-->
    <li>serketistBasis   -&gt;在神圣蜂巢女王的领导下，昆虫是银河系中完美的生命形式。</li>
    <!--EN: serketistFact    ->They are the pinnacle of evolution. [InsectAdjective]. [InsectAdjective2]. [InsectAdjective3]. Everyone should strive to become like them.-->
    <li>serketistFact    -&gt;它们是进化的顶峰。 [InsectAdjective]。 [InsectAdjective2]。 [InsectAdjective3]。每个人都应该努力成为像他们一样的人。</li>
    <!--EN: serketistProphecy->[itIsSaid] we will learn from them, becoming like a tidal wave that will wash over our enemies.-->
    <li>serketistProphecy-&gt;[itIsSaid]我们将向他们学习，变得像潮水一样冲垮我们的敌人。</li>
    <!--EN: itIsSaid->Perhaps, with time,-->
    <li>itIsSaid-&gt;也许，随着时间的推移，</li>
    <!--EN: itIsSaid->It is written in our destiny that-->
    <li>itIsSaid-&gt;我们的命运中写着：</li>
    <!--EN: itIsSaid->Either through technology or more arcane means-->
    <li>itIsSaid-&gt;通过技术或更神秘的手段</li>
    <!--EN: itIsSaid->We will revere their ways, their collective intelligence and-->
    <li>itIsSaid-&gt;我们将尊重他们的方式、他们的集体智慧和</li>
    <!--EN: itIsSaid->By revering the Will of the Hive Queen-->
    <li>itIsSaid-&gt;尊重蜂巢女王的意志</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective->Adaptive-->
    <li>InsectAdjective-&gt;自适应</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective->Ravenous-->
    <li>InsectAdjective-&gt;贪婪</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective->Overpowering-->
    <li>InsectAdjective-&gt;压倒性的</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective2->Versatile-->
    <li>InsectAdjective2-&gt;多功能</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective2->Uncompromising-->
    <li>InsectAdjective2-&gt;不妥协</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective2->Destructive-->
    <li>InsectAdjective2-&gt;破坏性</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective3->Complex-->
    <li>InsectAdjective3-&gt;复杂</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective3->Indestructible-->
    <li>InsectAdjective3-&gt;坚不可摧</li>
    <!--EN: InsectAdjective3->Resistant-->
    <li>InsectAdjective3-&gt;抵抗</li>
